<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.9.4: Solving for a Specified Variable</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00211</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.9.4: Solving for a Specified Variable</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c5654359-cfc3-4341-9aa3-e49fcff77931</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="practice" id="sect-00001"><title>Cool Down</title>
      <para id="para-00001">A school is holding a carnival and hopes to raise $500. Child tickets cost $3, and adult tickets cost $5. If the school sells <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> child tickets and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> adult tickets, then the equation <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>500</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> expresses the fact that the school raised exactly $500 from ticket sales.</para>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">Solve the equation for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Compare your answer:   <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mfrac><m:mrow><m:mn>500</m:mn><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:mfrac></m:mrow></m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00004">Explain when it might be helpful to rewrite the equation this way.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00005">Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. Solving for <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> helps us find out the number of child tickets to sell if we know the number of adults attending the carnival and we want to make exactly $500 from ticket sales.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
